Project 1 - Syringe Pump


Scope and Motivation

Line sterilization/flush requires an operator to manually inject large volume of SWFI into thin tubing. This is a time consuming process that takes effort, energy, and if done incorrectly can negatively impact the efficacy of the final drug product. Therefore, it is the scope of this project to assemble a syringe pump which will actuate the plunger via regulated air pressure in a safe and controlled manner to flush the lines with minimal operator interference. 

File Directory

For bill of materials and/or engineering drawings of the assembly go to BOM_specsheets. 
IRL pictures has some pictures of the progress and final assembly.
Old Versions is a part/STL graveyard of previous renditions of the assembly that were scrapped for one reason or another. 
Part file is where you can find manipulatable .SLDPRT(s) of the designed parts along with the .SLDPRT(s) acquired from McMaster-Carr for the final assembly.
STL file is where you can find the designed parts ready to be uploaded to a slicer for 3D printing.

Skills Used

3D Modeling with Solidworks

